WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:02.020
We're finally in the endgame now.

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:06.960
Following the world premiere of Avengers:
Endgame on Monday, April 22nd in downtown

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:12.380
Los Angeles, Marvel Studios lifted the social
media embargo on first reactions to the superhero

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.500
epic — spoiler-free, of course.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.400
Those fortunate enough to attend the screening
ahead of the film's theatrical debut later

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.970
this week raced to Twitter to pour out praise
by the bucketful, with critics, journalists,

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:27.860
and members of the media lionizing it as the
perfect culmination of the last 11 years of

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.380
the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:30.660
One common thread?

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.160
This movie is gonna make you cry like crazy.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.770
"This is a hot, hot movie.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:38.540
I didn't see the ending because I was crying
too much.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.320
I give it three hot, wet kisses."

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.460
Mashable's Angie J. Han, who admitted she
wasn't much of a fan of Infinity War, wrote

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:50.330
that Endgame is, quote, "an immensely satisfying
payoff, not just to Infinity War but to all

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:51.760
the films that came before (it)."

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:56.640
Brandon Davis of ComicBook.com had powerful
words to offer regarding Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:01.070
He tweeted, "#AvengersEndgame is an astonishing,
amazing film.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.850
I've never seen anything like it.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.440
This movie is everything I wanted to be and
SO much more.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:10.820
Amazing … While watching #AvengersEndgame,
I laughed so loud, I clapped with so much

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.720
force, and I cried so hard.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:17.500
The movie exceeds every expectation and is
the perfect culmination of the entire Marvel

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.620
Cinematic Universe."

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:24.790
Fandango managing editor Erik Davis also noted
that Endgame is a flawless, intelligent coming-together

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:29.160
of the 21 films that preceded it, further
teasing that the flick's ending is a rousing

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:29.660
one.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:34.760
"#AvengersEndgame is a masterful epic — a
true culmination of 22 films that not only

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.290
concludes the story, but expands upon it.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.840
You'll learn more about the other movies while
this one unfolds.

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:43.200
If Infinity War is the brawn, Endgame is the
brains.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.420
And wow, what an ending!"

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:48.460
He added in follow-up tweets that Endgame
stands as its own entity that complements

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:52.940
Infinity War, even though the two films were
shot back-to-back and do deal with the same

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:55.570
major threat in the intergalactic tyrant Thanos.

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:59.610
Meanwhile, audiences should be ready to check
their pride at the door and prepare to bawl

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:02.939
their eyes out and laugh hysterically while
watching Endgame unfold.

00:02:02.939 --> 00:02:05.920
"Do not go in expecting Infinity War part
two.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.840
The two films are so different, yet compliment
[sic] each other in all the best ways.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.750
In terms of which MCU movie to watch beforehand…
honestly, all of them.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.960
What an experience — what an accomplishment."

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:21.500
"Not going to spoil anything at all, but I
will say I laughed, I cried, I cried, I cheered,

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:26.870
I laughed, I cried again and then the entire
audience gave it a massive standing ovation.

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:28.120
And then I cried again.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:28.620
Be ready, kids.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:29.120
Be.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:29.620
Ready.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:30.180
#AvengersEndgame."

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:35.220
Peter Sciretta of Slashfilm tweeted that Avengers:
Endgame is incredibly emotional, apparently

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:39.239
due to both what happens within the film and
what the movie means to the larger picture

00:02:39.239 --> 00:02:40.239
of the MCU.

00:02:40.239 --> 00:02:46.560
"Imagine the best possible version of #AvengersEndgame
and somehow the film still surpasses all expectations.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.520
I cried 5-6 times.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.420
It's the most emotional, most epic, MCU film.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:56.680
A tribute to ten years of this universe and
holy shit the great fan service in this movie.

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:58.180
Soooo good."

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:04.280
Movie Trivia Shmoedown creator Kristian Harloff
agreed, writing, "Man #AvengersEndgame kicked

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:04.880
my ass.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.930
It was an epic conclusion to 11 years of films.

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:12.060
It had laughs, incredible action and absolute
emotional rollercoaster.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:15.980
It was the series finale for (this) cast of
characters that I had been hoping for.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:17.800
Congrats to all for pulling off the feat."

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:22.120
Beatrice Verhoeven, senior film reporter at
The Wrap, had something surprising to say

00:03:22.129 --> 00:03:25.910
to fans: none of the theories they came up
with have braced them for Endgame.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:29.540
"So I just saw #AvengersEndgame, and you guys
aren't ready for s***.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:32.260
All the theorizing didn't prepare you for
this.

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:35.980
I cried a lot, I flung my hands in the air
and screamed out loud.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:36.620
It's incredible."

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:40.820
Dave Itzkoff of the New York Times was so
emotionally involved in the film that he wound

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.560
up questioning his own parentage.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:47.470
"I was not prepared for the range of emotions
that #Endgame put me through, from utter despair

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:48.460
to pure elation.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:51.880
I laughed, I cried, I wished Tony Stark was
my dad."

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:55.000
Let's quickly check in with Tony Stark to
see how he feels about that.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:02.520
Dennis Tzeng of Collider Video praised Avengers:
Endgame as, quote, "an achievement in blockbuster

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:07.110
filmmaking," and said, "#AvengersEndgame is
filled with so much comic book awesomeness

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:08.460
that you may not be ready!"

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.780
Of course, not everyone completely freaked
the hell out on Twitter.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:16.680
Variety's Matt Donnelly kept his reaction
to Endgame simple but impactful: "Incredible

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:18.169
ingenuity and commitment.

00:04:18.169 --> 00:04:21.079
Marvel and Disney can and should be proud
of this moment."

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:25.280
Aaron Crouch of The Hollywood Reporter added
to the chorus of people singing Endgame's

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:29.380
praises noting that most of what fans have
seen of the film thus far through trailers

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:35.550
and TV spots barely scratches the surface
of the full flick: "90 % of the #AvengersEndgame

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:39.060
footage that's been officially released is
from the first 15 minutes: Other than the

00:04:39.060 --> 00:04:42.460
actual surprises, the biggest surprise to
me was how funny it is."

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:47.340
CinemaBlend's Eric Eisenberg offered a response
to Endgame that will give you chills: "This

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:51.580
can't be understated: #AvengersEndgame is
everything you want it to be and more.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.320
I am absolutely floored.

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:58.400
A perfect reflection on the last 11 years
that pays off everything in the best way possible.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:01.420
Without question my new favorite Marvel Cinematic
Universe film.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:01.920
Stunned."

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:07.080
Perri Nemiroff of Collider had a similar reaction,
though she warned that Endgame does, at times,

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.130
feel overwhelming.

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:11.970
In all, Nemiroff feels that everything leading
up to the film and to the film's conclusion

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:15.230
was worth it: "#AvengersEndgame is A LOT.

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:16.360
Too much at times.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:18.460
But wow the payoff is huge.

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:22.260
Left me proud to have invested over a decade
in a franchise that delivers an inspiring

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:25.449
exploration of what it means to be family
&amp; a hero.

00:05:25.449 --> 00:05:28.800
(Endgame also now has one of my favorite shots
in the entire MCU.)"

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.000
Hmmm...really?

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:30.920
Better than this shot?

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:40.120
Or this shot?

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:48.100
Overall, response to Avengers: Endgame has
been overwhelmingly positive.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:51.980
Critics have called it everything from the
"greatest superhero movie EVER" to "entertainment

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.860
from beginning to end" to "the film of the
year."

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:58.180
As always, though, these are just a selection
of reactions to a film that everyone is bound

00:05:58.180 --> 00:05:59.720
to have different opinions about.

00:05:59.890 --> 00:06:04.080
The fantastic feedback should make fans giddy
as they await the premiere of Avengers: Endgame

00:06:04.091 --> 00:06:08.250
on Friday, April 26, when they'll have the
chance to offer their own thoughts on the

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.250
superhero epic.

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:11.580
Until then, sit tight and avoid spoilers.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:15.850
And when the time comes, as one critic advised,
"plan your bathroom breaks accordingly."

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:17.740
And whatever you do...don't be like Iron Man.

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:21.300
"You know the question I get asked most often
is Tony, how do you go to the bathroom in

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:21.860
the suit...

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:26.720
just like that."

